=== Theoretical Analysis ===
n =  4:  log₂(n) = 2,  log₃(n) ≈ 2
n =  8:  log₂(n) = 3,  log₃(n) ≈ 2
n = 16:  log₂(n) = 4,  log₃(n) ≈ 3
n = 32:  log₂(n) = 5,  log₃(n) ≈ 4

=== Projected Scaling for Large Systems ===
n                  n  ceil(log2 n)  ceil(log3 n)
----------------------------------------------
100              100             7             5
1000            1000            10             7
10000          10000            14             9
